{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice because my interest in Eric Clapton makes the connection to JJ Cale especially appealing.",
    "A Hard Day's Night fits my interest in classic rock, although The Breeze is the stronger match for the one album I would choose today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The reggae, doo-wop, Motown, and funk collections miss my current interest in blues and guitar-led rock, even though they also feature established performers.",
    "Greatest Hits, Icon: The Hits, and Live At The Greek Theatre give me too little information about the performers to connect them to music I want to hear."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that interest in classic rock means I also want older music across many different styles.",
    "There is too much emphasis on hits collections; familiar songs alone do not make an album relevant to what I am seeking."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my recent Clapton listening and the blues-oriented appeal of JJ Cale matters more to me than an album's era.",
    "I rarely choose anything unless the connection to my current interests is clear, so a loosely related collection is unlikely to draw me in."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in classic rock but stretch it too broadly beyond the blues and guitar-led music I want right now."
}"}
